IntBSD i686 Operating System
----------------------------
IntBSD is a ix86 operating system built from scratch.
It uses the GNU GRUB bootloader.
Compiling IntBSD (ex. SwordXOS) involves in building a cross compiler, installing mtools, xorriso, grub and running several commands described in the Barebones Chapter of OSDev Wiki.
There is no official Installation script (yet).

So... how do i get it?
----------------------------
You could pick a prebuilt release or compiling it yourself.
If compiling:
     The following tools must be builded: i686-elf-gcc
     Build the following packages in the ~/opt/cross directory; ~/opt/cross/bin should contain i686-elf-* stuff.
     The following tools must be installed: GRUB, MTools, Xorriso, Git
     Example to install those tools on arch:
        sudo pacman -S grub mtools xorriso git
     Don't trust forks, but if you want to clone the fork:
        git clone https://github.com/imvariety/intBSD.git
     Cloning the original project:
        git clone https://github.com/sondaproject/intBSD.git
     In both of them you need to do:
        cd int*
     Finally build the kernel:
        ~/opt/cross/bin/i686-elf-gcc -T li*/li*ker.ld* -ffreestanding -nostdlib -O2 $(nproc) -lgcc -o myos k*/k*.c l*/l*.ld*
      You can now use grub-mkrescue to create a bootable image.
     
